{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>But if.</b> There is no doubt that there is no ransom for one put to death by the court. Therefore the translators of the religion [the Aramaic Targum] said that \"and he shall also be put to death\" means his death is by the hand of Heaven. Now this \"he shall be put to death,\" in my opinion, is like \"eye for eye\" — meaning it is fitting that he die if he does not give the ransom for his life and all this — because it is written יומת (\"he shall be put to death\") and not ימות (\"he will die\")."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:09.172688564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}